=== P2 Shared surface 0023 AILearnedAnomalyBaselines (Windows) ===

Capability: WinUI 3 (Windows App SDK) + .NET 10 present (dotnet 10.0.300; net10.0-windows10.0.19041.0
app TFM; Microsoft.WindowsAppSDK referenced). Build + headless logic tests run on this runner. The E2E
UI-automation runner (WinAppDriver/Appium) is ABSENT on this non-interactive host — see the TEST step.

Web source (THE spec): web/src/components/ai/AILearnedAnomalyBaselines.tsx, composed with the shared
web/src/components/ai/AIFeatureCard.tsx scaffold + web/src/components/ai/withAiFeature.tsx gate, streaming
web/src/hooks/useAiStream.ts (POST /api/v1/ai/ml/anomaly-baselines/train) into
web/src/components/ai/AiOutputPanel.tsx. The body is { vehicle_id: vehicleId ?? 0, days: 14 } and the
action is enabled by canStart = vehicleId != null.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE IMPLEMENTATION (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/AILearnedAnomalyBaselines.*)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Four-file split mirroring the shipped AnnouncerRegion / AICabinTemperatureImpactNarrative surfaces:
  .Model.cs      - Registration (slug AILearnedAnomalyBaselines, feature id
                   "learned-per-vehicle-anomaly-baselines", root automation id
                   ai-feature-learned-per-vehicle-anomaly-baselines-root, train path
                   /ai/ml/anomaly-baselines/train, DefaultLearningWindowDays=14, every i18n key+English
                   fallback); AnomalyBaselineStreamState enum (idle/streaming/paused-confirm/done/error -
                   the web AiStreamState union); AnomalyBaselineStreamEvent + AnomalyBaselineSseParser
                   (native port of useAiStream parseSSEFrame/toTypedEvent, malformed/unknown -> null,
                   bit-for-bit); AnomalyBaselineTrainRequest ({vehicle_id, days} - the web useMemo body,
                   snake_case JSON); PII-safe diagnostics (view.opened only).
  .Source.cs     - IAnomalyBaselineStreamTransport (P1/S8 seam = the native useAiStream) + production
                   HttpAnomalyBaselineStreamTransport (POST text/event-stream over HttpClient +
                   ITokenProvider, line-reassembled SSE frames; network faults -> classified terminal
                   Error event, never an exception across the enumerator; cancellation propagates).
                   IAnomalyBaselineFeatureGate (native useAiEnabled) + Static/Delegate gates.
  .ViewModel.cs  - INotifyPropertyChanged+IDisposable state machine: withAiFeature gate (IsGateOpen),
                   canStart guard (CanStart = vehicleId != null - web AILearnedAnomalyBaselines L53, NOT a
                   positive-id guard), useAiStream lifecycle (idle->streaming->done/error; duplicate Start
                   no-op; cancel->idle; close-without-terminal->done), offline classification, all
                   localized labels + the "Ask Helix . Train baseline" accessible name. Builds the request
                   with days=DefaultLearningWindowDays (14). Validates the feature id against the canonical
                   AiFeatureRegistry (native withAiFeature unknown-id guard).
  .cs            - WinUI 3 ContentControl: tokenized glass card (DisplayTokens), header (PanelTitle title +
                   "Helix" TsBadge + secondary description), TsButton (Outline/Small, IsLoading ring while
                   streaming), streamed-output panel (TsSpinner thinking indicator -> accumulating
                   narration -> danger error row), dispatcher-coalesced render, gate collapses the whole
                   surface when off (no root automation id - matches the web HOC rendering null), Narrator
                   name + Group automation peer, emits view.opened on Loaded.

States reproduced from the web source (every state renders; none hidden):
  gated-off (collapsed, no DOM/automation id) | idle not-ready (vehicle unresolved -> disabled action) |
  idle ready | streaming-thinking (spinner) | streaming-with-text | done (final narration) |
  error (Helix error: <msg>) | offline (connectivity fault -> offline message + retry via the button).
  NOTE: the web source is an on-demand SSE narration card, NOT a cached read; it has no data-freshness
  "stale" branch, so none is fabricated (faithful parity). The connectivity-aware "offline" branch is
  derived honestly from a classified network failure on the stream.

i18n: every string flows through ILocalizer.GetString(key, fallback) with the translation.* catalog
  prefix; keys: anomaly.aiBaseline.{title,description,generateButton,badge} (all four present in
  Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw), helix.{askHelix,thinking,errorLabel}, ai.common.errorUnknown,
  common.offline. English fallbacks verbatim from the web second args.
A11y: card Narrator name = title; action accessible name = "Ask Helix . Train baseline" (web aria-label);
  output panel is a live region; thinking spinner + error surface announce. No English literals in code.
Telemetry: view.opened slug=AILearnedAnomalyBaselines on Loaded (P1/S11), PII-safe (never the narration
  text, vehicle id, or prompt input).
Tests (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/AILearnedAnomalyBaselinesTests.cs, 43 cases):
  adapter unit tests (SSE parser delta/done/error/tool/confirm + malformed/unknown -> null, no-space,
  comment-line), the train-request body shape (vehicle_id + days=14), per-state view-model tests (gate
  on/off, canStart matrix [null->false, 0/-3/7->true], streaming->done, no-terminal->done, duplicate-start
  no-op, error, offline, confirm-pause, cancel->idle, retry), and a11y-label tests (action automation
  name "Ask Helix . Train baseline", thinking label flip, fallback copy). All via a headless fake transport
  + PassthroughLocalizer.

