PRE-EXISTING REPO FIXES required to reach a loadable/buildable gate (NOT part of the surface, but
mandatory to run build/test - documented per honesty covenant rule 7 "no predecessor bypass" / rule 9
"no silent drift"):
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was CORRUPTED into 5 concatenated <Project>
   roots (</Project> at lines 1132,1162,1165,1173,1179) by the file's documented `.gitattributes
   merge=union` strategy -> MSB4025 "multiple root elements" -> the WHOLE test project (and thus the
   `dotnet test` gate) could not load at HEAD. Regenerated, per the file's own INVARIANT, into exactly
   ONE <Project> = the verbatim singular header (Project + comment + PropertyGroup + the 3 unique
   PackageReference / 2 ProjectReference / 3 Content ItemGroups) + a single case-insensitive path-sorted,
   Include-deduplicated Compile-link ItemGroup of every Microsoft.UI-free .cs under dashboard-widgets/
   feature-views/misc-surfaces/modals-dialogs/shared-surfaces. 917 entries = the prior 914 unique union
   (980 raw - 66 merge duplicates) + this surface's 3 logic files (Model/Source/ViewModel; the bare WinUI
   view .cs stays in the app build). Verified: 1 <Project> open / 1 close, XML loads with a single root,
   917 Compile total == 917 unique.
2. The regenerated (now-loadable) build surfaced a latent type collision the csproj corruption had masked
   (the App project had never compiled): the VisuallyHidden surface (P2 shared-surfaces/0003) ships its own
   self-contained announcer stack, but its delegate `AnnouncerListener`, enum `AnnouncerPriority`, and class
   `AnnouncerRegionViewModel` collided (CS0101 x3 + CS0111 duplicate Dispose) with the sibling
   AnnouncerRegion surface's same-named public types in the shared TeslaSync.App.SharedSurfaces namespace,
   breaking BOTH TeslaSync.App.csproj (app) AND the test project. Fixed minimally + correctly by renaming
   ONLY VisuallyHidden's three colliding types to unique names (AnnouncerListener ->
   VisuallyHiddenAnnouncerListener, AnnouncerPriority -> VisuallyHiddenAnnouncerPriority,
   AnnouncerRegionViewModel -> VisuallyHiddenAnnouncerViewModel) across the four VisuallyHidden surface
   files + VisuallyHiddenTests.cs; AnnouncerRegion keeps the canonical names. Pure whole-word rename, zero
   behaviour change; restores the broken sibling surface to compiling. (Confirmed only these 2 type names
   were duplicated across all shared-surfaces sources; no external consumer references them.)

